cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite the archived release and the associated manuscript."
type: software
title: "leafwax-spatial: hierarchical Bayesian spatial calibration of leaf-wax hydrogen isotopes"
authors:
  - family-names: Bradley
    given-names: Alexander S.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4044-2802"
    affiliation: "Department of Earth, Environmental, and Planetary Sciences, Washington University in St. Louis"
    email: abradley@wustl.edu
abstract: >-
  Companion code for fitting hierarchical Bayesian spatial models that
  calibrate sedimentary leaf-wax n-C29 alkane hydrogen isotope ratios
  against precipitation isotope composition and environmental covariates.
  Implements 14 model variants in Stan with a Matern 3/2 Gaussian process
  predictive-process approximation on 125 globally distributed knots.
  Compares spatial and non-spatial calibrations across n = 1,128 surface
  sediment and soil sites from 73 publications.
keywords:
  - leaf wax
  - hydrogen isotopes
  - paleoclimate
  - Bayesian calibration
  - Stan
  - Gaussian process
  - spatial autocorrelation
  - hierarchical model
  - precipitation isotopes
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bradleylab/leafwax-spatial"
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: >-
      Geographic structure limits the generality of leaf-wax
      isotope–precipitation relationships
    authors:
      - family-names: Bradley
        given-names: Alexander S.
        orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4044-2802"
    year: 2026
